url: 'https://BAMresearch.github.io/bam-masterdata/'
abstract: >-
  bam-masterdata is an open-source Python package for defining,
  managing, validating, and exchanging metadata schemas used in
  the BAM Data Store, an institutional research data management
  infrastructure at the Federal Institute for Materials Research
  and Testing (BAM). The package provides reusable definitions
  of research objects, property types, and controlled vocabularies
  for materials science and engineering workflows. It supports
  version-controlled schema management, validation, and export
  to machine-readable formats, including JSON and RDF, as well as
  integration with openBIS. The project aims to facilitate
  metadata harmonization, interoperability, and FAIR-oriented
  research data management across heterogeneous scientific workflows.
keywords:
  - research data management
